      <div type="clause" n="8">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAtr">II Atr</ref> 8</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">[Be ðon ðe mon gefô ðe him losod wæs.] [Ld] Gyf hwa befo þæt him losod wæs, cenne se ðe he hit æt befo, hwanon hit him come; sylle on hand ⁊ sette borh, þæt he bringe his geteaman in ðær hit besprecen bið.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">If anyone attaches what he has lost, the man in whose possession it is attached shall declare how it came to him. He shall give pledges and furnish surety that he will produce his warrantor, when the case shall be brought into court.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Si quis deprehendat quod amisit, aduocet inde cum quo deprehenditur, unde uenerit ei; et mittat in manum et det plegium, quod adducet aduocatum suum.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
